  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q58-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "58",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{(x+1)(4x+1)}{x-1}$, $x\\ne\\frac14,1,-1$.\n\nFactorise the perfect square and differences of squares, then cancel common factors.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}&=\\frac{(x+1)^2}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{(4x-1)(4x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}&=\\frac{(x+1)(4x+1)}{x-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne\\frac14,1,-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
